From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:34:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] backend/drm: treat a gamma reset as a no-op on CRTCs without
 gamma

Resetting the gamma LUT on a CRTC that has neither a GAMMA_LUT property
nor a legacy gamma table (legacy_gamma_size 0, e.g. msm's MDP5) made
drm_legacy_crtc_set_gamma() fail without logging anything.

The scene re-applies the gamma LUT when an output is enabled again,
which adds a color transform reset to the state. wlr_output_test_state()
drops that field because it is unchanged, so the test passes, but
wlr_backend_commit() keeps it and the real commit fails. With sway,
'output X power on' after 'power off' therefore failed once with
"Backend commit failed" and only worked on the second try.

There is nothing to reset on such a CRTC, so report success.
---
 backend/drm/legacy.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/backend/drm/legacy.c b/backend/drm/legacy.c
index 714addb..a152ff3 100644
--- a/backend/drm/legacy.c
+++ b/backend/drm/legacy.c
@@ -255,7 +255,8 @@ bool drm_legacy_crtc_set_gamma(struct wlr_drm_backend *drm,
 		// The legacy interface doesn't offer a way to reset the gamma LUT
 		size = drm_crtc_get_gamma_lut_size(drm, crtc);
 		if (size == 0) {
-			return false;
+			// The CRTC has no gamma LUT, so there is nothing to reset
+			return true;
 		}
 
 		linear_lut = malloc(3 * size * sizeof(uint16_t));
